1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,064
REA Safe Agent is a skill that builds a
safer,

2
00:00:03,064 --> 00:00:06,460
contained environment for analyzing files
with REA.

3
00:00:06,960 --> 00:00:10,761
Use it when your agent must analyze a file
you don't trust.

4
00:00:10,761 --> 00:00:14,690
That file can hand the agent instructions,
not just evidence.

5
00:00:15,190 --> 00:00:16,477
Pick one archive.

6
00:00:16,477 --> 00:00:22,610
REA opens it, lists its contents and
closes it; your agent explains the
evidence.

7
00:00:23,110 --> 00:00:27,304
Only reviewed copies, pinned by size and
hash, reach REA.

8
00:00:27,304 --> 00:00:29,880
Your original folder stays outside.

9
00:00:30,380 --> 00:00:34,317
REA and your agent run in separate
restricted containers.

10
00:00:34,317 --> 00:00:36,320
The agent has no host mounts,

11
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:39,843
and the host controller allows only
approved tools,

12
00:00:39,843 --> 00:00:42,260
including read-only Ghidra queries.

13
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:45,205
Neither container has external network.

14
00:00:45,205 --> 00:00:47,587
Each agent uses your own subscription,

15
00:00:47,587 --> 00:00:52,100
and what it reads from your approved files
can reach your model service.

16
00:00:52,600 --> 00:00:54,752
The file is never executed.

17
00:00:54,752 --> 00:00:58,100
Risk goes down, but it never reaches zero.

18
00:00:58,600 --> 00:01:00,241
Verify the boundaries.

19
00:01:00,241 --> 00:01:02,180
Repeat after every change.
